# groovy-f: f folds Groovy and Jenkinsfiles (#1347). On a stage's first line f folds the stage
# and f there unfolds it; on a line inside a sh ''' string f folds the step around it. The file is
# written here, not in the project, which every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p ci && printf "node('linux') {\n    stage('build') {\n        sh '''\n            make all\n        '''\n    }\n}\n" > ci/Jenkinsfile
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl ci/Jenkinsfile
wait A Jenkinsfile
key :
type 2
key Enter f
wait 3 lines ⋯ }
key f
wait make all
key :
type 3
key Enter f
wait 2 lines
key q
wait merl exited: 0
